  ],
  "details": "<p>According to\u00a0<span>La Trobe and Niblett (2016), this site was significantly damaged by the construction of Georgian houses and then by the construction of <span>the Spa Treatment Centre\u00a0</span>built in\u00a0</span>the nineteenth century. On the site were the remains of three roads and three masonry buildings designated A, B, and C. The site produced a quantity of window glass as well as some finer quality stone. Possible evidence of a formal garden was also noted.</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Site of masonry buildings in Aquae Sulis, modern-day Bath.",
